[{"id":"smq-year1-1.38-q1","number":1,"question":"<h3>Applications of Differentiation</h3><p>For each of the following situations, find the first differential, explain what it means in context and specify its units:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C=5.8x+14.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where \u00a3<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the cost of the transport and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the miles travelled.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=-t^2+6t+135\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the height of a ball (in metres) and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of seconds passed.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=0.01t^3-0.2t^2+20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the temperature (<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"{}^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>C) of a substance and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number hours that have passed.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dC}{dx}=5.8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For each additional mile travelled, the cost increases by \u00a35.80</p>","<p>Units: \u00a3/mile</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dt}=-2t+6\\quad\\text{so}\\quad\\left.\\frac{dh}{dt}\\right|_{t=10}=-14\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> exactly, the height of the ball is decreasing at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"14\\ \\mathrm{ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Units: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dT}{dt}=0.03t^2-0.4t\\quad\\text{so}\\quad\\left.\\frac{dT}{dt}\\right|_{t=5}=-1.25\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> exactly, the temperature of the substance is decreasing at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.25{}^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>C per hour.</p>","<p>Units: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"{}^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>C per hour</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.38-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>The spread of a virus over a period of 22 days may be modelled by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"N=-0.49t^2+10t+3.54\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of people with the virus and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of days passed. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the rate of spread of the virus on day 5</p></li><li><p>the rate of spread of the virus on day 15</p></li><li><p>the coordinate of the maximum of the curve of the model giving the points to 3 significant figures.</p></li><li><p>explain the meaning of the maximum point you found in part c)</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dN}{dt}=-0.98t+10\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dN}{dt}\\right|_{t=5}=5.1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>On day 5 there is 5.1 people per day gaining the virus</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dN}{dt}\\right|_{t=15}=-4.7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>On day 15 there is 4.7 fewer people per day gaining the virus</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Max pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dN}{dt}=0\\ \\therefore -0.98t+10=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(10.2,54.6)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>The model says that at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=10.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> days, the maximum amount of people with the virus is 54.6 people.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.38-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>The height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of a seedling in mm is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h=-0.028n^2+1.95n+6.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of days passed.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dn}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and state its physical relevance.</p></li><li><p>Use this model to predict the day at which the seedling reaches maximum height and state its height.</p></li><li><p>How effective is the model in the long term?</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dn}=-0.056n+1.95\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>It represents the rate in change (per day) of the height of the seedling (in mm)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Max when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dn}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-0.056n+1.95=0\\ \\therefore n=34.8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So according to the model during the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"34^{\\mathrm{th}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> day it reaches its maximum height of 40.2 mm</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The model is no longer valid after reaching its maximum because it then models the height as decreasing.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.38-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>The velocity of an object over <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds may be given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"v=\\frac73t^3-8t^2+4t+10,\\qquad 0\\leq t\\leq3\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is velocity in metres per second.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the coordinates of the stationary points of the model giving your answer to 3 significant figures.</p></li><li><p>Explain the meaning of stationary points in the context of the object.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dv}{dt}=7t^2-16t+4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dv}{dt}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7t^2-16t+4=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore t=2,\\ t=\\frac27\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(2,4.67),(0.286,10.5)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=13\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Therefore when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds the object has its lowest velocity, and when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.286\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds, the object has a local maximum velocity (the actual maximum is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"13\\ \\mathrm{ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.38-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>The depth of water <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm below a model boat at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds is modelled by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=t^3-8t^2+15t+48,\\qquad0\\leq t\\leq5\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the greatest depth of water below the model boat.</p></li><li><p>Find the minimum value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dt}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the time at which it occurs and the depth of the water at this time.</p></li><li><p>State the vertical direction the boat is moving at the time found in part b)</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dt}=3t^2-16t+15\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dt}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3t^2-16t+15=0\\ \\Rightarrow\\ t=\\frac83\\pm\\frac13\\sqrt{19}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\frac83-\\frac13\\sqrt{19}=1.21\\ \\mathrm{s}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=56.2\\ \\mathrm{cm}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=5\\ \\mathrm{s}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=48\\ \\mathrm{cm}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> maximum depth of water is 56.2 cm</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3t^2-16t+15\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Min when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6t-16=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\frac83=2.67\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right|_{t=\\frac83}=-\\frac{19}3=-6.33\\quad(3\\ \\mathrm{SF})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=50.1\\ \\mathrm{cm}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The boat is moving downwards as this point happens after the local maximum.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.38-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>A model for the height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of a roller coaster in feet is</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h(x)=2x^3-30x^2+94x+150\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the horizontal distance in hundreds of feet. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the gradient of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the angle of inclination (in degrees) to the ground of the rollercoaster initially.</p></li><li><p>the highest point of the rollercoaster and where they occur, giving your answer to the nearest feet.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h'(x)=6x^2-60x+94\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h'(0)=94\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Initially, the gradient says that for every 100 feet the height of the rollercoaster increases by 94 feet</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{94}{100}\\right)=43.2{}^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Max and min heights when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h'(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6x^2-60x+94=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=5\\pm\\frac23\\sqrt{21}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Max when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1.944949537\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>The maximum height occurs 194 feet horizontally from the beginning of the rollercoaster and reaches a height of 234 feet above the ground.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.38-q7","number":7,"question":"<h3>Applications of Integration</h3><p>The height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of a pile of sand above ground level can be modelled by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h(x)=-10x^3+14x^2+\\frac32x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of metres from one side. The mean height of the pile of sand may be given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=\\frac12\\int_0^2h(x)\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\int_0^2-10x^3+14x^2+\\frac32x\\,dx=\\left[-\\frac54x^4+\\frac73x^3+\\frac38x^2\\right]_0^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=\\left(-20+\\frac{56}3+\\frac32\\right)-(0)=\\frac16=0.167\\text{ metres}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.38-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>The value of some shares \u00a3<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\" data-display=\"false\"></span> during the first 12 months of the year may be modelled by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V(t)=0.5t^3+3.5t^2-12t+50\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of months passed.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use this model to predict the value of the shares when 12 months have passed.</p></li></ol><p>The mean share of the shares value may be given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=\\frac1{12}\\int_0^{12}V(t)\\,dt\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>\u00a31274</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac1{12}\\int_0^{12}0.5t^3+3.5t^2-12t+50\\,dt\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=\\left[\\frac1{96}t^4+\\frac7{72}t^3-\\frac12t^2+\\frac{25}6t\\right]_0^{12}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=(216+168-72+50)-(0)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=362\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So \u00a3362</p>"]}]